+# ATLAS R1 — HUMAN AWE FIRST / PUBLIC EXPERIENCE P0 — 08 OCT 2026
+
+**STATUS:** IMPLEMENTED + TESTED LOCALLY / CANDIDATE DELIVERY AGAINST HEIR `king/test@5dc63fe8ddd1daea32d62d102066705d3c7efbfe` / NOT MERGED / NOT DEPLOYED / FOUNDER iPHONE REVIEW PENDING.
+
+**AUTHORITY:** Founder ATLAS master execution pack 07 Oct 2026 + AXE answers 07 Oct 2026 (three releases; R1 first; `4planetatlas.com` owns ATLAS + PLACE in search) + Brand OS with Founder Brand Reset 05 Oct 2026 (fresh-read from Drive `1bOIr3a83N53RVFZs_jibXr02cRS_RSP_bhCDVmN0_88`).
+
+**BRAND OS PREFLIGHT:** user job — see what the living planet holds at a place, in a person's words · brand mode — REDUCED / MORE ICONIC utility surface around one immersive element · dominant idea — THE EARTH IS THE HERO · dominant visual anchor — the globe in its own dark space · obvious next action — search, or tap Earth · living-world presence — ENCOUNTER (the planet itself; documentary species photograph where the source licenses one) · active contextual accent — 4PLANET Blue, on Paper only, for the one decisive action (Brand OS §15.2A) · type hierarchy — Instrument Sans 26/24 display (weight 500), DM Sans 16/15/13.5/12.5 reading and interface, Fragment Mono 12/10.5 for identifiers at evidence depth only (7 levels) · grid / whitespace — one 384px column beside Earth on wide screens, one sheet beneath it on compact screens, 16/20px gutters · geometry — one radius family 12 / 22 / capsule, one elevation, two line strengths · deliberately deferred — weather, local time, NOW geographic relevance, TIME model, COMPARE, global place search (geocoder needs a rights decision).
+
+## USER ARRIVES BECAUSE
+They searched for a place, a species or a planetary phenomenon and landed on ATLAS from Google, on a phone, never having heard of 4PLANET.
+
+## ONE THING TO UNDERSTAND
+This is an interactive view of the living planet: tap or search anywhere and see what has actually been recorded there, with where it came from.
+
+## PRIMARY ACTION
+Search a place or species — or tap anywhere on Earth.
+
+## SECONDARY DEPTH
+More (relationships, pressures, reported events) on request; then SOURCES AND LIMITS: exact source, query geometry, counts, identifiers, check times and every caveat, one tap away on every object.
+
+## P1 DOMINANT
+Earth. Resting chrome (wordmark, search line, dock, zoom) covers under a fifth of a 390×844 screen.
+
+## P2 ORIENTATION
+A plain kind word and a name ("Marine area · Oslofjord", "Species · Orca", "Here · Near Larvik"), one human sentence, and the species with the most records in the area by common name.
+
+## P3 ACTION / NEXT
+Follow (the one blue action) and "More about …", both reachable without scrolling; four dock doors — Now, Layers, Watch, My Atlas.
+
+## P4 DEPTH
+Identifiers, coordinates, bounding-box caveats, record counts, source links, review/evidence axes, per-source coverage (Layers → Sources and coverage), layer source/time-class/legend/opacity.
+
+## WHAT CAN BE REMOVED
+Removed: the all-mono uppercase console voice; internal ids, coordinates, SEEDED/LIVE badges and BOUNDING BOX rows on the first read; separate floating Layers and My Atlas buttons; the EARTH lens button (closing a surface IS Earth); the duplicated desktop wordmark; the status strip readout; the unused `atlasPolish.css` override sheet and its body-wide MutationObserver sidecar; the `window.fetch` interception sidecar; a second basemap style load at every boot; a full basemap re-style on every panel open/close.
+
+## WHAT MUST BE REUSED
+One MapLibre engine, one ContextLayer, one layer registry, one signal pool, one camera authority, the existing follow / saved-view / 4PLANET ID stores, the existing `/api/atlas-feed` and `/api/atlas-wms` bridges, the shared typographic product switcher, Brand OS type and colour tokens. No parallel Context engine, no second design system, no new source.
+
+## TRUTH BOUNDARY
+Hide complexity, never hide uncertainty. A gap (source unavailable, nothing returned, not checked, no coverage, bundled-not-live) is spoken in words on the first read; a sound section carries its origin as a caption and its provenance in SOURCES AND LIMITS. Query area ≠ place membership; a tapped point is named only by the nearest basemap label WITH its distance, or not at all; "most recorded" is a statement about records in a query area, not a species list; source failure ≠ zero; LIVE only for a genuinely live source; nothing is promoted to an alert.
+
+## MOBILE-FIRST RISK
+A control floating over a sheet; iOS focus-zoom leaving the page panned; a sheet covering the thing selected; touch targets under 44px; text under 12px; horizontal overflow; search results under the keyboard; map not recovering after repeated surfaces. Each is covered by `tests/e2e/atlas-r1-human-awe.spec.ts` at 390×844 and 430×932 except real-device Safari and the real keyboard, which remain human gates.
+
+## HUMAN SUCCESS
+A person who has never heard of 4PLANET opens ATLAS on a phone and, without instruction, searches or taps, reads what lives there in ordinary words, sees where that came from when they ask, follows something, and comes back. Technical PASS is not this; Founder iPhone review on `test.4planet.org/atlas` and observed users decide it.
+
+**DONOR DECISION:** none adopted. The unmounted `atlasPolish.css` / `AtlasHumanSurfacePolish.tsx` donor layer is REJECTED WITH REASON (an `!important` correction sheet plus a body-wide MutationObserver — the pattern this release retires) and removed.
+
+**RELEASE:** delivered as a versioned patch against the exact HEIR parent. AXE owns apply, sandbox-registry reconciliation, final gates, deploy, Search Console and public LIVE verification.
+
+---
+
